Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables & columns  
• GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER.REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS  
  – "creative_page_url" : page URL of each removed ad  
  – "region_stats" (VARIANT) : contains “region_code”, “first_shown”, “last_shown”, “times_shown_lower_bound”, “times_shown_upper_bound”, “times_shown_availability_date”, … – used for HR filtering and impression‑range checks  
  – "disapproval" (VARIANT) : nested object that stores “removal_reason”, “violation_category”, …  
  – "audience_selection_approach_info" (VARIANT) : for demographic_info, geo_location, contextual_signals, customer_lists, topics_of_interest – used to be sure at least one is not “NOT_USED” (or similar)  

Principal conditions we will need later  
• rs.value:"region_code" = 'HR'  
• rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date" IS NULL  
• rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::INT  > 10000  
• rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::INT  < 25000  
• At least one of these is not “CRITERIA_NOT_USED” (or “NONE”) → audience_selection_approach_info:"demographic_info", ...  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively inspect the data and finally satisfy all requested filters.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes.

